# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
title    Nests
composer Claude
about    Webs from wall to wall and something moving in every one of them: a thin fiddle in C minor over a harpsichord that never stops scurrying, a dark string pad, a low wordless choir and an upright bass on every beat. Db and a diminished chord pull at the key. When something is near, a hi-hat ticks like many legs over a low tom heartbeat and timpani; brass joins the fight, a full choir and gong come for a guardian.
tempo    100
beats    4
steps    4
reverb   0.45

# moods (music/README.md)
# mood explore:  lead harpsi strings bass voices
# mood treasure: harpsi strings voices wonder
# mood sense:    hat toms timpani strings bass voices
# mood rise:     sense lead harpsi kick snare
# mood fight:    rise -voices -harpsi -hat -snare brass drive war crash
# mood boss:     fight -lead choir gong

voice lead     fiddle      vol=0.5  pan=-0.15 rev=0.45
voice harpsi   harpsichord vol=0.42 pan=0.3
voice strings  strings     vol=0.24 pan=-0.25 center=G3 att=0.4 rel=0.8
voice bass     upright     vol=0.7
voice voices   voices      vol=0.26 pan=0.1  att=0.6 rel=1
voice wonder   musicbox    vol=0.3  pan=0.45 rev=0.7
voice hat      hat         vol=0.35 pan=0.35
voice toms     tomlo       vol=0.55 pan=-0.2
voice timpani  timpani     vol=0.5  pan=-0.1
voice kick     kick        vol=0.55
voice snare    snare       vol=0.38 pan=0.1
voice brass    brass       vol=0.45 pan=-0.25 gate=0.65 center=G3 att=0.018 rel=0.09 rev=0.22
voice crash    crash       vol=0.28 pan=0.2
voice choir    choir       vol=0.32 center=C4 att=0.4 rel=0.8
voice gong     gong        vol=0.3  pan=-0.3

# Combat-only motion: tight low ostinato and accented battle drums, at the same tempo.
voice drive    pizz      vol=0.5  pan=0.3 gate=0.5 rev=0.2
voice war      snare     vol=0.44 pan=0.15 rev=0.2

